    <item>
      <title>WIP: Minimal Distro</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/minimal-distro/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:18:10 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/minimal-distro/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;wip-assembling-a-minimal-distro&#34;&gt;WIP: Assembling a Minimal Distro&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;table-of-contents&#34;&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#the-why&#34;&gt;The Why?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#what-is-a-linux-distribution&#34;&gt;What is a Linux Distribution?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#requirements&#34;&gt;Requirements&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#why-actual-hardware&#34;&gt;Why Actual Hardware?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#understanding-the-boot-process&#34;&gt;Understanding the Boot Process&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#set-up-the-workspace&#34;&gt;Set Up the Workspace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#configuring-and-building-the-linux-kernel&#34;&gt;Configuring and Building the Linux Kernel&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#creating-the-composition-of-the-initramfs&#34;&gt;Creating the Composition of the initramfs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#creating-the-composition-of-the-rootfs&#34;&gt;Creating the Composition of the rootfs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#storage-layout-on-the-usb-drive&#34;&gt;Storage Layout on the USB Drive&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#installing-grub&#34;&gt;Installing GRUB&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#flashing-the-software-image&#34;&gt;Flashing the Software Image&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#booting-the-hardware-with-the-new-distro&#34;&gt;Booting the Hardware with the New &amp;ldquo;Distro&amp;rdquo;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#transitioning-from-initramfs-to-rootfs&#34;&gt;Transitioning from initramfs to rootfs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#bring-up-complete&#34;&gt;Bring-Up Complete&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#what-next&#34;&gt;What Next?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-why&#34;&gt;The Why?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There are many classes of computing devices, ranging from small handheld mobile devices to servers, that are said to run &amp;ldquo;Linux.&amp;rdquo; However, the phrase &amp;ldquo;It runs Linux&amp;rdquo; is often used without clearly defining what it means. Does it mean that the device runs just the Linux kernel, or does it mean something more, such as a Linux distribution (whatever that means)?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
